      "explanation": "Full credit (1 point) for correctly explaining Kariuki's purpose for publishing the song. Acceptable responses (NYSED rating guide) include: to promote African unity/Pan-Africanism; to show the problems of European imperialism; to show Africa's history of struggles for freedom; to celebrate the independence of Egypt/Ethiopia/Ghana; to motivate Africans to continue the struggle in Kenya/South Africa; to highlight the suffering caused by colonialism; to express the thoughts of Kenyan political prisoners; to call for a United States of Africa; or because a largely illiterate population could understand a song. Not acceptable: to justify colonialism, to show European favor, or 'he was a political activist.'",
